# Template for ~/.config/yadm/leak-patterns (copy it, uncomment, fill in).
#
# One extended regex per line, matched case-insensitively. Blank lines and #comments are ignored.
# These are the things that must never appear in anything pushed to a PUBLIC remote: file contents,
# file paths, commit authors/messages, and diffs. Used by the pre-push hook and by
# ~/.agents/skills/manage-dotfiles-repo/scripts/leak-scan.
#
# The real file is private by nature (it names the very things that must not leak), so keep it on a
# private branch only, never on a branch that goes to a public remote.
#
# Ideas: your surname, your employer's name, internal hostnames and domains, internal repo paths,
# ticket-project prefixes, internal package-index hosts.
#
#surname
#employername
#internal\.example\.com
